From 93aaab93eaee5c2f5e1d652f6e57c89c6d6e579d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:04:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 134/135] media: i2c: add an OmniVision OV64B40 driver

Add a driver for the OmniVision OV64B40 64 MP sensor with one fixed
mode: 4624x3472 RAW10, the full array binned 2x2, over three C-PHY trios
at 1.684 Gsps (link frequency 842 MHz) from a 19.2 MHz MCLK.

The tables are the vendor initialisation and mode sequences of the
Xiaomi Redmi Note 12 Turbo wide module. The per-module calibration
blocks that the vendor writes from the module EEPROM (0x5a40, 0x5f80,
0x6141) are not written. After stream on the vendor sequence writes
0x3019 and 0x4308; the driver does the same.

The register map follows the OV64A40: exposure 0x3500 (lines), analogue
gain 0x3508 (code / 256 here, up to 0x0ff0 as the vendor driver uses),
digital gain 0x350a (1x), frame length 0x3840/0x380e, the group hold
sequence 0x3208 = 0x00, 0x10, 0xa0, and the test patterns at 0x50c1.
The chip ID register 0x300a reads 0x5664 in its upper 16 bits, as the
vendor driver checks.

The pixel rate is the C-PHY payload rate, 1.684 G * 16 / 7 * 3 / 10 =
1154.7 Mpixel/s; the read-only horizontal blanking makes the 3628-line
frame 30 fps in those pixels.

Power sequencing follows the vendor module: reset asserted, AVDD, DVDD
and DOVDD, MCLK, reset released 10 ms later and 8 ms before the first
register access. Runtime PM autosuspends after 2 s and keeps the sensor
off for at least 1.2 s: a Qualcomm CCI master that stays clocked across
a sensor power cycle hangs until it reinitialises on runtime resume. The
chip ID is checked again at stream start, with one retry.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig   |   12 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile  |    1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/ov64b40.c | 2696 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 2709 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/ov64b40.c

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
index 19d5f2dab0..1ffb483afc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
@@ -665,6 +665,18 @@ config VIDEO_OV64A40
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
 	  module will be called ov64a40.
 
+config VIDEO_OV64B40
+	tristate "OmniVision OV64B40 sensor support"
+	depends on OF && GPIOLIB
+	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+	help
+	  This is a Video4Linux2 sensor driver for the OmniVision
+	  OV64B40
+	  camera.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called ov64b40.
+
 config VIDEO_OV7251
 	tristate "OmniVision OV7251 sensor support"
 	help
